WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.000
Today, Web DSH, Web Terminal, and installed managed clients operate in the user's private workspace.

00:09.000 --> 00:19.000
DSH chat, the DSH Python SDK entry point, and Claude Code are separate clients. Chat does not forward work to another client.

00:19.000 --> 00:29.000
The approved target design adds two independent web choices: agent runtime and execution backend.

00:29.000 --> 00:40.000
DSH Python SDK supports programmatic workflows; Claude Code supports repository work. Private DSH workspace remains the default backend.

00:40.000 --> 00:50.000
OpenShell is optional, disabled, and unavailable until its isolation, rollback, resource, and expiry gates pass.

00:50.000 --> 01:00.000
The planned web task form and guarded Claude flow are not deployed yet; acceptance work remains.
